Midden

The Midden core and the skills of the Midden bundle are distributed under the
license in LICENSE.

The Midden app is powered by Compa (https://github.com/xibodev/compa), an
MIT-licensed agent runtime. The app ships Compa's compa-kernel program
unchanged from Compa's own release, with Compa's LICENSE and NOTICE in
app/compa. The app artifact's app/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt names Compa and the
other components from the same team in one line each, and includes the
licenses of the other modules compiled into midden-ui and compa-kernel.

The installer's app mode downloads Pandoc (https://github.com/jgm/pandoc,
GPL-2.0-or-later) from Pandoc's own release, checks it against the SHA-256 in
Midden's release manifest and keeps it in app/tools for the app's agent.
Midden does not redistribute Pandoc.

Core artifacts contain their own THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and do not embed
Compa or model-provider runtimes. Dependency notices are generated from the
module graph used for the corresponding artifact, not from user data.

The generated Kagi API client's pinned module declares Apache-2.0 in its
shipped api/openapi.yaml rather than in a standalone license file. Release
notices identify that declaration and include the standard license text from
licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.
